-- int-tests-register: headline (b), whole scenarios across groups G1 (Article 1 "registered charity", the entity), G2 (IP10: the charity test only by virtue of an Order), G3 (the register), G5 (IP29),
-- G7 (commencement, the text of the Law) and G8 (IP19 the required steps notices, IP20 organized religious charities).  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from Articles 1, 8, 9 and 10 before this module was run:
--   Article 1: "registered charity" means an entity entered for the time being in the general section or the restricted section of the register (the historic section is not in it);
--   Article 8(3): for each registered charity the register holds (a) the note of status, (b) the governors' names, (c) the principal address, (d) other premises in Jersey if any, (e) the registered charitable purposes,
--   (f) the registered public benefit statement, (g) the date registered, (h) a note if an organized religious charity, (i) the text of the constitutional provision if the test is met by an Order under Article 5(3),
--   (j) whether the annual return for the most recent year has been sent, (k) a note of any required steps notice and its date, (l) previous names if the name changed, (m) details under an Order under Article 13(9)(c), (n) other prescribed information;
--   Article 8(5): for a formerly registered charity in the historic section (a) the former number, (b) the name(s) if registered in the general section, (c) a summary of the reason, (d) the dates registered and deregistered, (e) other prescribed matters;
--   Article 9(1): the public elements of the restricted section are (a) the number but not the name, (b) the matters under 8(3)(a), (e), (f), (j) and (k), (c) a summary of reasons produced by the charity, (d) other prescribed elements.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (b): scenarios`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

-- Two lists hold the same items, whatever their order.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      expected IS A LIST OF a
      actual IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the same items` expected actual MEANS
        count expected EQUALS count actual
    AND all (GIVEN x YIELD elem x actual) expected

GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the registered school company` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
        standing IS `entered in the general section`
        purposes IS LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`))
        facts IS `Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "A. Le Brun"))
        model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
        people IS LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "A. Le Brun")

GIVETH A `Register entry in the case`
`the register entry of the school company` MEANS
    `Register entry in the case` WITH
        body IS `the registered school company`
        `charity test facts` IS `Int fx the charity test facts with` `Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided`
        placements IS LIST (`Int fx a placement in` `the general section` (YMD 2019 3 1))
        `registration number` IS "C-0412"
        `registered name` IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "to advance education in Jersey"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "Free schooling for children in Jersey"
        `Order under Article 28` IS `Int fx no Order under Article 28`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the items of Article 8(3)` IS `Int fx clear facts for the items of Article 8(3) with the address` "1 Esplanade, St Helier"
        `facts for the items of Article 8(5)` IS `Int fx facts for the items of Article 8(5) with the placements` EMPTY
        `facts for the public elements` IS `Int fx facts for the public elements with a summary of reasons`
        `facts for the principal address` IS `Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` "1 Esplanade, St Helier"
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

§§ `B1: a charity registered in the general section, no notice, nothing out of the ordinary`

-- Registered 1 March 2019; asked on 2 October 2026. Article 1: an entity in the general section is a registered charity. Article 8(3) requires (a), (b), (c), (e), (f), (g) and (j); (d) there is no other premises,
-- (h) not organized religious, (i) the test is not met by an Order, (k) no notice, (l) the name has not changed, (m) no Order under 13(9)(c), (n) nothing prescribed.
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of the school company`)'s `the entity is a registered charity`
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of the school company`)'s `section the entity is entered in` EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of the school company`)'s `the recorded standing agrees with the entries`
#ASSERT `the same items` (LIST `a note of the status of the entity`, `the names of each of the governors`, `the principal address`, `the registered charitable purposes`, `the registered public benefit statement`, `the date on which the charity was registered`, `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`) ((`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of the school company`)'s `the entries the Commissioner must enter`)
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of the school company`)'s `the addresses that may be entered as the principal address` EQUALS LIST "1 Esplanade, St Helier"
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of the school company`)'s `the entries the Commissioner must enter in the historic section` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of the school company`)'s `the public elements of the restricted section` EQUALS EMPTY

