§§ `B4: a charity in the restricted section -- the public elements -- Article 9(1)`

GIVETH A `Register entry in the case`
`the register entry of a restricted section charity` MEANS
    `Register entry in the case` WITH
        body IS `Body in the case` WITH
            name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
            standing IS `entered in the restricted section`
            purposes IS (`the registered school company`)'s purposes
            facts IS (`the registered school company`)'s facts
            model IS (`the registered school company`)'s model
            people IS (`the registered school company`)'s people
        `charity test facts` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `charity test facts`
        placements IS LIST (`Int fx a placement in` `the general section` (YMD 2019 3 1)), (`Int fx a placement in` `the restricted section` (YMD 2022 6 1))
        `registration number` IS "C-0412"
        `registered name` IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "to advance education in Jersey"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "Free schooling for children in Jersey"
        `Order under Article 28` IS `Int fx no Order under Article 28`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the items of Article 8(3)` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
        `facts for the items of Article 8(5)` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the items of Article 8(5)`
        `facts for the public elements` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the public elements`
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

-- Entered in the restricted section on 1 June 2022: a registered charity (Article 1), section restricted. The public elements are (a) the number (not the name), (b) the matters under 8(3)(a), (e), (f) and (j) -- (k) there is no notice --
-- and (c) the summary of reasons, produced by the charity.
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a restricted section charity`)'s `the entity is a registered charity`
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a restricted section charity`)'s `section the entity is entered in` EQUALS JUST `the restricted section`
#ASSERT `the same items` (LIST `the registration number, but not the registered name`, `the note of status registered under Article 8(3)(a)`, `the registered charitable purposes registered under Article 8(3)(e)`, `the registered public benefit statement registered under Article 8(3)(f)`, `the note of the annual return registered under Article 8(3)(j)`, `a summary of the reasons for registration in the restricted section`) ((`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a restricted section charity`)'s `the public elements of the restricted section`)
-- Asked about 31 May 2022, the day before the entry: still in the general section.
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2022 5 31) `the register entry of a restricted section charity`)'s `section the entity is entered in` EQUALS JUST `the general section`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2022 5 31) `the register entry of a restricted section charity`)'s `the recorded standing agrees with the entries`

§§ `B5: a formerly registered charity in the historic section -- not a registered charity -- Article 8(5)`

GIVETH A `Register entry in the case`
`the register entry of a deregistered charity` MEANS
    `Register entry in the case` WITH
        body IS `Body in the case` WITH
            name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
            standing IS `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
            purposes IS (`the registered school company`)'s purposes
            facts IS (`the registered school company`)'s facts
            model IS (`the registered school company`)'s model
            people IS (`the registered school company`)'s people
        `charity test facts` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `charity test facts`
        placements IS LIST (`Int fx a placement in` `the general section` (YMD 2019 3 1)), (`Int fx a placement in` `the historic section` (YMD 2025 6 1))
        `registration number` IS "C-0412"
        `registered name` IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date deregistered` IS JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "to advance education in Jersey"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "Free schooling for children in Jersey"
        `Order under Article 28` IS `Int fx no Order under Article 28`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the items of Article 8(3)` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
        `facts for the items of Article 8(5)` IS `Int fx facts for the items of Article 8(5) with the placements` (LIST (`Int fx a placement in` `the general section` (YMD 2019 3 1)))
        `facts for the public elements` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the public elements`
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

-- Trap T7: the historic section holds formerly registered charities, and "registered charity" does not take it in. So the entity is on the register but is not a registered charity: nothing is owed under Article 8(3).
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a deregistered charity`)'s `the entity is a registered charity`
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a deregistered charity`)'s `section the entity is entered in` EQUALS JUST `the historic section`
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a deregistered charity`)'s `the entries the Commissioner must enter` EQUALS EMPTY
-- Article 8(5): (a) the former number, (b) the name(s) (it was in the general section), (c) the reason, (d) the dates. (e) nothing prescribed.
#ASSERT `the same items` (LIST `the entity's former registered number`, `the name under which the entity was registered immediately before deregistration, and the names under which it was previously so registered`, `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`, `the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered`) ((`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a deregistered charity`)'s `the entries the Commissioner must enter in the historic section`)
-- The day before deregistration (31 May 2025) the same entity was in the general section: a registered charity again.
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2025 5 31) `the register entry of a deregistered charity`)'s `section the entity is entered in` EQUALS JUST `the general section`

§§ `B6: a charity that meets the test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3) -- Article 8(3)(i)`

GIVETH A `Register entry in the case`
`the register entry of a charity controlled by a Minister under an Order` MEANS
    `Register entry in the case` WITH
        body IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s body
        `charity test facts` IS `Facts for the charity test in the case` WITH `constitution facts` IS `Int fx a constitution permitting control by a Minister`, `public benefit determination` IS `Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided`, `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies Article 5(2) for the entity` IS TRUE
        placements IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s placements
        `registration number` IS "C-0412"
        `registered name` IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `alternative registered names` IS EMPTY
        `date registered` IS YMD 2019 3 1
        `date deregistered` IS NOTHING
        `registered charitable purposes` IS LIST "to advance education in Jersey"
        `registered public benefit statement` IS "Free schooling for children in Jersey"
        `Order under Article 28` IS `Int fx no Order under Article 28`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the items of Article 8(3)` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the items of Article 8(3)`
        `facts for the items of Article 8(5)` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the items of Article 8(5)`
        `facts for the public elements` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the public elements`
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the register entry of the school company`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

-- The constitution expressly permits a Minister to control the entity, in that capacity: Article 5(2) bars the test, and an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies the bar. The charity meets the test only by virtue of the Order,
-- so the register holds the text of the provision (Article 8(3)(i)).
#ASSERT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a charity controlled by a Minister under an Order`)'s `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order`
#ASSERT elem `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)` ((`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of a charity controlled by a Minister under an Order`)'s `the entries the Commissioner must enter`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the register entry of the school company`)'s `the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order`

§§ `B7 and B8: the day`

-- Part 4 came into force on 1 May 2018: on 30 April 2018 Article 8 is not in force. After it, before 1 January 2019, no text of the Law is among the sources and group G1 refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30) `the register entry of the school company` BECAUSE "Article 8 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (b) is the entity a registered charity and what does the register hold` fleet (YMD 2018 6 1) `the register entry of the school company` BECAUSE "no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources"
-- The standing the register records disagrees with the dated entries: the answer says so (the integrator's check of IP6 and IP7).
